# ===== Private submodule =====
# `internal/` is a separate private repo mounted as a submodule via .gitmodules.
# `git submodule add` stages it bypassing this rule; this entry only prevents
# accidental tracking of internal/ contents before submodule init.
internal/

# ===== Public/private placement guard =====
# These are maintainer/agent working materials. Their canonical home is the
# private internal/ submodule; ignoring them here prevents an accidental
# reintroduction after the public/private split. CI independently audits the
# tracked tree, so `git add -f` cannot bypass the boundary silently.
/docs/plans/
/docs/archive/
/docs/baselines/
/docs/superpowers/
/docs/Architecture/
/docs/CODING_RULES/
/.planning/
/rules/
/HANDOFF.md
/PROJECT_MAP.md
/TODO.md
/REFACTOR_STATUS.md
/tools/update_engine.py

